<rml>
<head>
	<title>Generic Confirm Dialog Background</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="generic_confirm_dialog_bg.rcss"/>
</head>
<body>
	<!-- Background-context document (see npc_shop_bg.rml for the mechanism) -- paints the panel's
	     own frame/fill BEFORE the legacy 3D pass draws item3D each frame (RenderBackgroundLayer(),
	     called from CManager::Render() before any window/camera in its z-sorted loop), so the item
	     shows through the gap in generic_confirm_dialog.rml's own now-paint-less #panel instead of
	     being painted over by it (RmlUi's main context, rendered last in the frame, would otherwise
	     always win). No data-model -- #panel centers via plain CSS
	     (left:50%;top:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-50%)), unlike npc_shop_bg's own
	     root_x/root_y/root_scale data-style bindings: this dialog's position is never
	     C++-computed the way an inventory-family window's is, so there's nothing to sync per
	     frame. -->
	<div id="panel">
		<div class="gcd-bg-shell-edge"></div>
		<div class="gcd-bg-groove"></div>
		<div class="gcd-bg-content-fill"></div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
